 <script lang="ts">
   import { selection } from '$lib/logic/selection';
+  import { saveToCloud, cloudSyncStatus } from '$lib/cloud-sync';
   // ... existing imports

+  // Add cloud save option to existing save functionality
+  async function saveToCloudStorage() {
+    const files = get(selection).files;
+    for (const [fileId, file] of files) {
+      if (file) {
+        await saveToCloud(file, file._data.name || `track-${fileId}.gpx`);
+      }
+    }
+  }
 </script>

--- Apply Instructions ---
1. Create the cloud-sync.ts file in website/src/lib/
2. Import cloud-sync functions into SaveButton.svelte
3. Add "Save to Cloud" button/option in the save dialog
4. Add "Open from Cloud" option in the file open dialog

Note: The local Dexie storage is preserved for instant operations.
Cloud sync happens explicitly when user chooses to save/load from cloud.
